new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5e41352
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SUMMARY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Summary
+
+**Changed**
+- `stockreport/report.py`: `render()` handles `"markdown"`. It uses the vendored `tabulate` with `style="pipe"` and `number_format=".2f"`. It then adds a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `markdown` as well as `text`.
+- `README.md`: documents the new option.
+- No existing tests, `vendor/` files or dependencies were touched. I added no new tests, because `tests/test_report.py` already covers this output.
+
+**Verified**
+- `python -W error -m unittest` ran 3 tests, all OK. That includes the existing markdown and CLI markdown tests, and no DeprecationWarnings were raised.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown` printed the expected table and total (461.93).
+- The text format output is unchanged.
+
+**Not verified**
+- I only tried `inventory.csv`. Item names containing `|` are not escaped, so they would break the markdown table. The vendored library does not escape them and I did not work around that.
